# PostgreSQL 18 + pgvector 0.8.7 + Apache AGE 1.8.0: the "one engine" rival to
# the cross-model transaction (pgvector hit, Cypher hop through AGE, row update,
# one transaction). Base image pinned by digest; AGE from the PGDG apt repo the
# postgres image already carries. Built as dbbench:pg-age by build_images.sh.
#
# MOVED TO PG18 ON 2026-09-19 WITH THE REST OF THE POSTGRESQL SET (DECISIONS
# #87, #103d: one engine wears one version per page). postgres, pgvector and
# TimescaleDB moved to their pg18 builds in the same commit, and THIS image is
# the one that gated the set: AGE is the only one of the four packaged per
# PostgreSQL major, so the set could only move once PGDG carried an AGE build
# for 18. It does -- 1.8.0~rc0 on apt.postgresql.org, bookworm and trixie --
# and the extension version is read back onto the row at connect, so the row
# records what was installed rather than what this file asked for.
#
# BOTH AGE ENDPOINTS ARE ~rc0 DEBIAN PACKAGES, and that is not a regression:
# the PG17 pin this replaces was 1.7.0~rc0. Apache AGE tags every release -rc0
# and votes that artifact through as the release, so there is no non-rc build
# to pin to and "latest stable" for AGE means the newest -rc0 for the major.
#
# MOVED TO POSTGRESQL 18.7 ON 2026-11-25 (humemai/mmdbbench#114, #175; the owner: "I go with your recommendations"). The base is the 0.8.7-pg18
# build of 2026-11-12, whose image reads PG_VERSION=18.7-1.pgdg12+2 (the registry config), from `pgvector/pgvector@sha256:ad249f9fb957...` on
# PostgreSQL 18.6. The AGE package moves with it, from 1.8.0~rc0-2.pgdg12+1 to 1.8.0~rc0-2.pgdg12+2: PGDG rebuilt AGE for 18.7 (the +2 build
# declares `Depends: postgresql-18 (>> 18.7)`, the +1 build `postgresql-18`), and PostgreSQL 18.7's release notes say a minor release
# changes the server's ABI for C-language extensions. Same AGE version (1.8.0, read back onto every row), so the rows still say age:1.8.0.
# PostgreSQL 19.0 is NOT used: Apache AGE supports PostgreSQL up to 18 (comparator_constraints.json).
#
# THE PACKAGE IS PINNED TOO (2026-10-02, CAMPAIGN section 7 row 26). The base
# image is pinned by digest, but `postgresql-18-age` unversioned took whatever
# PGDG served on the build day, so two builds of this file could carry two
# AGE builds under one tag. Pinned to the build the cross-model rows were
# measured on (`dpkg-query` on dbbench:pg-age: 1.8.0~rc0-2.pgdg12+1, which the
# rows record as age:1.8.0). If PGDG stops serving it, the build fails here
# rather than moving AGE silently.
FROM pgvector/pgvector@sha256:4bdc16048580b56345bca441bffe8d9b45dd2f5d76963808c853df1661df6e00
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends postgresql-18-age=1.8.0~rc0-2.pgdg12+2 \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
